# Normalise line endings in the repository regardless of each contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, whether a file lands in git with CRLF depends on
# the machine that committed it - this repo is authored on Windows (autocrlf=true) and
# would be cloned on Linux, so leaving it to config invites spurious whole-file diffs.
* text=auto

# Binary payloads git must never touch. papers/*.pdf is gitignored, but fetch_papers.py
# writes there and a stray `git add -f` must not corrupt a checksum-verified download.
*.pdf binary

# Read as text but keep LF: JSON manifests and golden sets are compared byte-for-byte by
# tests, and shell scripts must stay LF to remain runnable on POSIX.
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
